MultiThreading
--------------

Multitasking is divided into two types Process based multitasking and thread based multitasking.
Executing several tasks simultaneously where each task is separate independent process such type of multitasking is
called Process based multitasking.
Process based multitasking best suited at Operating system level not at program level.

Executing several tasks simultaneously where each task is a separate independent process of the same program such
type of multitasking is called Thread based multitasking. Each independent part is called Thread.
The main objective of multitasking is to reduce response time of the system and to improve performance.

The main important application areas of multithreading are

    1. To develop multi-media graphics
    2. To develop animations
    3. To develop video games
    4. To develop webservers and application servers etc.,

A Thread is a separate flow of execution of a program.
We can define a thread in 2 ways.

    1. by extending Thread class
    2. by implementing Runnable interface

Thread scheduler is part of the JVM it is responsible to schedule threads that is if multiple threads are waiting to
get chance of execution the order in which threads will be executed is decided by Thread scheduler.
We can't except exact algorithm followed by Thread scheduler it is varied from JVM to JVM hence we can't expect thread
execution order and exact output